  <page_number>163[?]</page_number>
  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Y</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Tales, &amp; humano cruore altaria</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Fœdare, contentus iugulatis bestiis:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Quid? nonne deuouit Cainum atrocibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Diris, &amp; esse iussit omnibus sagum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Trepidúmque terris, quòd suum peremerat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Fratrem? Ipse sero si meum crudelior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Occido natum, nonne crimen turpius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Meum sequetur &amp; sque pœna tristior?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Quo me trepidum procella rursus abripis? An</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>qua Superi mandant, vocare somnia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Quis audet, atque ludicras imagines?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Quid non homo inuenit, suas coram Deo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Dum quaerit excusare frustra callidus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Rebelliones! Da seniam parens bone.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Meum necari filium imperas! tibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Parebitur iamiam: patris casus manu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Te sic volente Isacus immolabitur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">SATHANAS.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Adhuc supersunt machinæ quibus illius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Tentabo pectus obstinatum impellere,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Mirum nisi tandem fatiscens corruat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">ABRAHAMVS.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>At, ô, meum si maćto filium effluent</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Promissa in auras facta quondam: nec tuis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>[?]osthac habebitur fides sermonibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>[?]enigne Cœlitum parens. Venientibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>[?]eclis Isacum pluribus prædixeras</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>[?]atrem futurum gentibus, quæ totum [?]er</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>orbis incolæ plagas [?]ellent tuis</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Left edge is clipped, so the first letters of several lines (Posthac, Benigne, Ecclis, patrem, per) are doubtful. "maćto" as printed; "sellent" may be "vellent". The page number could read 168 rather than 163.</notes>
</page>
